# Synced from exmateria-sound + project-assets by tools/sync_exmateria_sound.sh.
# These are populated artifacts, not source — repopulate with the sync script.
# Both spellings: a rsync'd copy is a directory, but a linked worktree makes
# these SYMLINKS, and a trailing-slash pattern does not match a symlink.
/addons/exmateria_sound/
/addons/exmateria_sound
/addons/exmateria_spu/
/addons/exmateria_spu
/assets/music/

# Per-scenario event-script chunk JSONs (~212 MiB, all 500 TEST.EVT events),
# consumed by the F3 scenario picker. Deterministically regenerable:
#   uv run python tools/export_all_scenario_chunks.py
# The default cinematic falls back to the committed scenario_1_chunk.json when
# this dir is absent, so a fresh clone still plays without generating them.
/assets/scenarios/chunks/

# {7D} ShowGraphic textures (chapter cards, ending stills, GAME OVER, 131 WLDBK
# world backgrounds) — ~5 MiB, decoded straight from EVENT/*.BIN + WORLD/WLDBK.BIN.
# Regenerate: uv run python tools/parse_show_graphics.py
/assets/scenarios/graphics/

# {91} ShowMapTitle location-name strips (115 inked, 256x20 4bpp) decoded from
# EVENT/MAPTITLE.BIN + the map_titles.json manifest (incl. the map_id->slot table,
# derived map_id-1 per the ATTACK.OUT worker). Regenerate:
#   uv run python tools/parse_map_titles.py
/assets/scenarios/map_titles/

# {50} Portrait Row EVTFACE event-dialogue portraits (64-cell 8x8 grid) — decoded
# straight from EVENT/EVTFACE.BIN. Regenerate: uv run python tools/parse_evtface.py
/assets/scenarios/faces/

# Derived character-alignment templates (ADR-0072 / wayfinder #200): one folder
# per template key (res://assets/characters/templates/<token>/), each an owned
# sliced asset packet (body/portrait/formation + events/, + template.json).
# ROM-derived + git-lfs-sized, NOT committed. Regenerate: run the transform then
# `godot --path . --import`. Loaders fall back to the flat assets/sprites/textures
# store when a folder is absent, so a fresh clone still renders. Schema:
# docs/TEMPLATE_JSON_SCHEMA.md.
/assets/characters/templates/

# Shared generic events store (wayfinder #206): SPR-pooled cinematic EVTCHR frames
# owned by job-class generics / non-residue sprites, one folder per resolved SPR
# (res://assets/characters/generics/<HEX>/events/chr/ + generic.json). ROM-derived,
# regenerated by the same transform, NOT committed.
/assets/characters/generics/

# Transform-internal event-asset derivation (wayfinder #204): the recovered
# segment->character residue the ROM never stored, written by
# align_character_templates.py alongside the templates. ROM-derived + regenerable
# (rerun the transform), NOT a runtime read surface — gitignored like the templates.
/assets/scenarios/event_asset_map.json

# Crystal ({92} SS=1) frames extracted from BATTLE/OTHER.SPR — regenerable.
# Regenerate: python3 tools/extract_crystal.py
/tools/crystal_out/

# Pace-comparison scratch: raw PSX-vs-Godot timeline captures + Godot's generated
# .translation/.import artifacts. Throwaway probe output, regenerated on demand.
/tmp_pace/

# The tunable registry snapshot (ADR-0068 addendum M4): a regenerated dev artifact
# dumped in-game as the bridge to the materialize codemod. NOT a source of truth —
# and neither is config/tune_overrides.json, which stopped being tracked on 90e593900
# and is ignored from the REPO-ROOT .gitignore. Both are machine-scoped dev artifacts;
# godot-learning ADR-0281 is why a test process may not read or write either.
/config/tune_registry.snapshot.json

# Effect Studio Save output (game→json→bin repack; never the pristine extract)
/authored_effects/
tools/.touch_cache.json

# World-map screen: WLDTEX.TM2 replayed into a VRAM image + the WLDCORE model,
# both produced by tools/parse_world_map.py. ROM-derived and regenerable.
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH, and that is load-bearing: `/assets/world_map/` matches a
# DIRECTORY only. Worktrees populate this path by symlinking it at a sibling, and the
# moment it is a symlink instead of a directory the trailing-slash form stops matching,
# so an ordinary `git add -A` sweeps a machine-specific absolute path into the tree.
# That is exactly how one got committed to `main` and self-referenced in the worktree
# it named — at a time when NOTHING automated made the link and every worktree that
# wanted the world map made it by hand.
#
# tools/link_worktree_godot_assets.sh now links this path with the rest, but the
# slash-less rule is deliberately kept as the primary defence rather than leaning on
# that script's own trap-handler (it records every path it linked into a managed block in
# the worktree's LOCAL .git/info/exclude). This rule is TRACKED and mechanism-independent:
# it holds for a hand-made link, for a worktree the script was never run in, and for whatever
# populates the path next. The exclude list only holds where the script ran. When a new
# generated path needs the same protection, write it here without the slash first.
/assets/world_map

# The {78} Display Conditions screens: EVENT/BONUS.BIN's 36 pages decoded to the
# results font sheet + the 36 victory-condition banners, plus the overlay tables
# read out of EVENT/REQUIRE.OUT. Produced by tools/parse_bonus.py, ROM-derived and
# regenerable.
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH, for the reason spelled out at /assets/world_map above: a
# worktree may populate this path with a SYMLINK, and `/assets/scenarios/results/`
# would stop matching the moment it is one.
/assets/scenarios/results

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MOVED HERE FROM THE MONOREPO ROOT `.gitignore`'s `# === godot-learning ===`
# section, with the prefix stripped. Every rule below was package-scoped and
# spelled `godot-learning/…`, which is a path that does not exist in the
# standalone `exmateria-gambit-tactics` repo this package ships as.
#
# 🔴 That was not cosmetic. `assets/effects/*`, `assets/sprites/textures/`,
# `assets/sprites/animations/`, `assets/maps/` and `assets/fonts/*` are the
# bulk ROM derivations. With the rules left upstairs, a standalone clone
# ignores NONE of them and the first `git add -A` after a bootstrap commits
# Square Enix data — the one thing decision 2 of the extraction plan forbids.
#
# Git reads a `.gitignore` relative to its own directory, so these mean the
# same thing here as they did at the root. Verified by comparing
# `git status --ignored` over the package, before and after: same 488 paths.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Godot editor cache
.godot/

# Editor-specific settings
.vscode/settings.json

# Temporary/debug files
src/camera_ref.gd
**/logs/
**/*.bak

# User-specific settings (not committed)
user_settings.json

# Tune's AUTOSAVE sink. The game rewrites this on essentially every boot (any
# Tune.Persist.AUTOSAVE slug a debug panel touches), so as a TRACKED file it made
# every `git pull` on a shared worktree fail on unstaged changes, and a test that
# drove a real debug panel could silently rewrite another developer's pins (see
# Tune.gd's commit_slug docs for the incident). tools/materialize_tunables.py still
# reads it from disk, so the ADR-0068 R6 scrub -> drain-into-code workflow is
# unaffected; only the sharing of a local staging file is.
config/tune_overrides.json

# Stale test logs (do not commit)
test_results/

# Python tools virtual environment
tools/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Generated sound samples (extracted from WAVESET.WD)
assets/sounds/samples/
assets/sounds/waveset_index.json

# Regression test results (generated, not committed)
tests/results/

# Generated assets from FFT extract parsing — regenerate with tools/
#
# 🔴 `assets/characters/templates/` (163 files) was ignored by NOTHING TRACKED.
# `align_character_templates.py:40` says the tree is "generated + gitignored
# (`/assets/characters/templates/`)" and `bootstrap_assets.sh:364` writes it, but
# the only rule covering it was line 19 of this clone's `.git/info/exclude` —
# untracked, per-checkout, written by tools/link_worktree_godot_assets.sh. It is
# shared across this clone's worktrees, which is exactly why it looked covered
# everywhere anyone checked. A fresh clone does not have it, so a bootstrap
# followed by `git add -A` committed 163 ROM derivations.
# Both spellings: a linked worktree makes this a SYMLINK, and a trailing-slash
# pattern does not match a symlink.
assets/characters/templates/
assets/characters/templates
assets/sprites/textures/
assets/sprites/animations/
assets/sprites/layer_priority.json
assets/maps/
assets/effects/*
assets/fonts/*
!assets/fonts/font_atlas.tga.import
assets/ui/*
!assets/ui/*.json
assets/items/item_icons*.tga
assets/items/item_icons*.tga.import

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE BLOCK BELOW LIVES HERE, NOT IN THE MONOREPO ROOT `.gitignore`, and the
# paths in it are PACKAGE-relative with no `godot-learning/` prefix.
#
# This file ships as-is into the standalone `exmateria-gambit-tactics` repo via
# `git subtree`, where the package IS the repo root. A rule spelled
# `godot-learning/assets/…` matches nothing there, and a second, prefixed copy
# at the monorepo root would make this file differ between the two repos —
# which is a permanent merge conflict on every sync, and the one thing the
# subtree decision (handoff 1, decision 1) exists to avoid.
#
# Git reads a `.gitignore` relative to its OWN directory and lets a deeper file
# override a shallower one, so these rules mean the same thing in both repos
# and still beat the root file's `!godot-learning/assets/ui/*.json` negation.
# Verified with `git check-ignore -v` over all 56 paths, before and after.
#
# KEEP THIS BLOCK LAST. It re-ignores individual artifacts that the broader
# rules above negate — `assets/ui/dialog_triangle.json` against
# `!assets/ui/*.json` — and within one .gitignore the LAST matching pattern
# wins. Ordered the other way, two artifacts silently stopped being ignored;
# it showed up as a `??` in a before/after `git status --ignored` diff and in
# nothing else.
#
# No leading `/`: a pattern containing a slash is already anchored to this
# directory, and a leading one would have to be stripped back off by
# tools/check_generated_assets.py before it could match a manifest row.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BEGIN generated-assets (rendered from tools/data/generated_assets.tsv)
# Root ADR-0001: disc-derived artifacts are rebuilt by
# tools/bootstrap_assets.sh, never committed. Listed one path per
# line rather than by glob, because several of these directories mix generated
# artifacts with hand-authored ones (assets/ui/, assets/scenarios/,
# addons/exmateria_almanac/sprites/) and a glob would take the authored files
# with it. Placed last so it wins over the broader `!`-negations above.
#
# Do not hand-edit: re-render from the manifest. check_generated_assets.py fails
# if this block and the manifest disagree.
addons/exmateria_almanac/abilities/AbilityDatabase.gd
addons/exmateria_almanac/abilities/AbilityView.gd
addons/exmateria_almanac/encounters/battle_conditionals.json
